# Enter and Tab in the kinds of paragraph an HTML message has.

== Enter at the end of a heading starts normal text
modes: html
markdown: # Title
caret: end
keys: {ENTER}
type: next
markdown-is: # Title\n\nnext

== Enter in the middle of a heading leaves two headings
modes: html
markdown: # OneTwo
caret: after "One"
keys: {ENTER}
markdown-is: # One\n\n# Two

== Enter in a bulleted list starts a new item
modes: html
markdown: - one
caret: end
keys: {ENTER}
type: two
markdown-is: - one\n- two

== Enter on an empty list item leaves the list
modes: html
markdown: - one
caret: end
keys: {ENTER}
keys: {ENTER}
type: after
text-is: one\nafter
markdown-is: - one\n\nafter

== Tab in a list item nests it and Shift+Tab brings it back
modes: html
markdown: - one\n- two
caret: end
keys: {TAB}
focus-is: Message body
markdown-is: - one\n  - two
caret: end
keys: +{TAB}
focus-is: Message body
markdown-is: - one\n- two
typing-works

== Enter in a quote continues the quote
modes: html
markdown: > one
caret: end
keys: {ENTER}
type: two
markdown-is: > one\n>\n> two

== Enter on an empty quoted line leaves the quote
modes: html
markdown: > one
caret: end
keys: {ENTER}
keys: {ENTER}
type: after
markdown-is: > one\n\nafter

== Enter in a code block adds a line to the block
modes: html
markdown: ```\nline one\n```
caret: after "line one"
keys: {ENTER}
type: line two
markdown-is: ```\nline one\nline two\n```

== Enter on an empty last line of a code block leaves the block
modes: html
markdown: ```\nline one\n```
caret: after "line one"
keys: {ENTER}
keys: {ENTER}
type: after
markdown-is: ```\nline one\n```\n\nafter

== A table is one cell per line
modes: html
markdown: | Name | Size |\n| --- | --- |\n| One | 12 |
text-is: Name\nSize\nOne\n12\n
caret: before "Name"
keys: {DOWN}
caret-is: before "Size"
keys: {DOWN}
caret-is: before "One"

== Enter in a table cell starts a new line in the same cell
modes: html
markdown: | Name | Size |\n| --- | --- |\n| One | 12 |
caret: after "One"
keys: {ENTER}
type: more
markdown-is: | Name | Size |\n| --- | --- |\n| One more | 12 |

== Backspace at the start of a table cell does not merge it with the cell before
modes: html
markdown: | Name | Size |\n| --- | --- |\n| One | 12 |
caret: before "Size"
keys: {BACKSPACE}
markdown-is: | Name | Size |\n| --- | --- |\n| One | 12 |

== Delete at the end of a table cell does not merge it with the next cell
modes: html
markdown: | Name | Size |\n| --- | --- |\n| One | 12 |
caret: after "Name"
keys: {DELETE}
markdown-is: | Name | Size |\n| --- | --- |\n| One | 12 |
typing-works

== Inline code survives into what is sent
modes: html
markdown: Some `inline code` here
text-is: Some inline code here
markdown-is: Some `inline code` here

== A code block keeps its font, so it is still a code block when sent
modes: html
markdown: ```\nline one\nline two\n```
markdown-is: ```\nline one\nline two\n```

== Bold switched on straight after a switch to HTML applies to what is typed
# In a window that has just opened: the HTML editor is made by this switch and is still loading
# when Ctrl+B is pressed.
fresh
modes: plain
keys: ^+3
keys: ^b
type: bold
keys: ^b
wait: 2.5
mode-is: html
text-is: bold
markdown-is: **bold**

== Bold switched on straight after each switch to HTML, three times over
modes: plain
keys: ^+3
keys: ^b
type: one
keys: ^b
markdown-is: **one**
keys: ^a{DELETE}
keys: ^b
type: two
keys: ^b
markdown-is: **two**
keys: ^a{DELETE}
keys: ^+1
wait: 1
keys: ^+3
keys: ^i
type: three
keys: ^i
markdown-is: *three*
